[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4500930327","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119605#issuecomment-4500930327","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119605","id":4500930327,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDEa_Fw","user":{"login":"passivestar","id":60579014,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNTc5MDE0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60579014?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar","html_url":"https://github.com/passivestar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-20T17:32:52Z","updated_at":"2026-05-20T17:32:52Z","body":"You'd normally have the decal at geometry surface so the arrow will be inside of the geometry. Maybe drawing that arrow at the outer gizmo boundary would make more sense?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4500930327/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4501014079","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119605#issuecomment-4501014079","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119605","id":4501014079,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDEgGPw","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-20T17:44:02Z","updated_at":"2026-05-20T17:44:25Z","body":"> You'd normally have the decal at geometry surface so the arrow will be inside of the geometry. Maybe drawing that arrow at the outer gizmo boundary would make more sense?\r\n\r\nThis makes sense, as this could also encourage not making the decal's gizmo extents too tall (since the arrow would end up far away from the surface it's projecting on). To improve performance, you want to keep the decal extents as small as possible without affecting visuals so it can be culled earlier when the camera rotates away.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4501014079/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4501255470","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119605#issuecomment-4501255470","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119605","id":4501255470,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDEu1Lg","user":{"login":"passivestar","id":60579014,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNTc5MDE0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60579014?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar","html_url":"https://github.com/passivestar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-20T18:11:18Z","updated_at":"2026-05-20T18:11:18Z","body":"What if decal's default y size was halved? it would serve both as a hint that the box should be flat (in most cases) and an additional orientation guide besides the arrow","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4501255470/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4501575464","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119605#issuecomment-4501575464","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119605","id":4501575464,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDFCXKA","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-20T18:46:16Z","updated_at":"2026-05-20T18:46:37Z","body":"> What if decal's default y size was halved?\r\n\r\nI've been thinking about changing some Decal defaults for nodes newly created in the editor to improve usability, but this will be in a separate PR. (Existing nodes would keep their defaults to preserve compatibility.)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4501575464/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4502456029","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119605#issuecomment-4502456029","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119605","id":4502456029,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDF4G3Q","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-20T20:39:43Z","updated_at":"2026-05-20T20:42:48Z","body":"Moved the arrow to the outer gizmo boundary:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"972\" height=\"688\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4001bd11-91be-40d3-b07d-22f30eb23aa5\" />\r\n\r\nBy the way, I was thinking there should be some kind of indication of \"this way up\". This way, when a decal is pointing downwards, you can know whether you've rotated it the right way around. Maybe draw a smaller caret pointing upwards next to the directional arrow?\r\n\r\nThe idea is to have something similar to Camera3D with the triangle on the top:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"425\" height=\"329\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7e9b640f-632a-4d69-bcb6-214502890623\" />\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4502456029/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4504570386","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119605#issuecomment-4504570386","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119605","id":4504570386,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDH5KEg","user":{"login":"passivestar","id":60579014,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNTc5MDE0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60579014?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar","html_url":"https://github.com/passivestar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-21T03:40:29Z","updated_at":"2026-05-21T03:40:29Z","body":"Can't hurt, but if you can't tell if a decal is upside down just by looking at the decal then it probably doesn't matter that it's upside down","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4504570386/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4512156911","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119605#issuecomment-4512156911","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119605","id":4512156911,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDPIM7w","user":{"login":"JekSun97","id":130399274,"node_id":"U_kgDOB8W8Kg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/130399274?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97","html_url":"https://github.com/JekSun97","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-21T19:39:51Z","updated_at":"2026-05-21T19:46:09Z","body":"> The idea is to have something similar to Camera3D with the triangle on the top\r\n\r\nI think the Gizmo option, similar to Camera, looks more appropriate, although it clutters up a little more space, it accurately shows the direction, and could also show the size and distance.\r\n\r\nBut then it would be logical for the texture to be projected as indicated by the Gizmo, as happens with SpotLight3D and with the light_projector texture enabled, but this is hardly the purpose of Decal.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4512156911/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4536136511","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119605#issuecomment-4536136511","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119605","id":4536136511,"